  fixed while building

    * http_core emit() keyed the body write off the request
      method, so every POST reply sent Content-Length and then
      no body. Clients hung until timeout. The flag is now a
      separate send argument, which also makes HEAD correct.

  checked by hand

    * health open, every /api route 401 without the token
    * wrong token 401, token comparison is constant time
    * /ui traversal to /etc/passwd blocked, 404
    * /api/doc restricted to the generated file list, 404 on
      ../../etc/passwd
    * Range 10-19 returns 206 with 10 bytes, past-end gives 416
    * body over 1 MiB gives 413
    * config patch rejects unknown keys, wrong types and both
      secret keys, and never echoes a secret back
    * HTTP/1.1 keep-alive holds across three pipelined requests
    * config survives restart, written 0600

  notes

    * admin token is generated on first run and printed once per
      start. UI will not load without it.
    * server binds 127.0.0.1 only. tunnel must mount /alexa and
      /audio and must NOT mount /ui or /api.
    * cfg keys for F04..F09 already exist in the defaults table so
      the UI can show them before those features land.


