  fixed while building

    * src/queue.py shadowed the stdlib queue module, which broke
      urllib3 inside ytmusicapi with "module 'queue' has no
      attribute 'LifoQueue'". Renamed to qu.py, and cookies.py
      to ck.py for the same reason. There is now an import audit
      that loads every module next to yt_dlp and ytmusicapi.
    * yt-dlp exited 1 while still producing a correct file: the
      -o template ended in .part and collided with yt-dlp's own
      partial file handling. Now downloads to tmp-<vid>.m4a and
      renames, with temp files swept on every path.
    * the first scorer had no relevance term at all and ranked
      on view count, so "mujhe maaph karna" picked a 196M view
      song that was not the one asked for. Added the fold based
      title coverage term, cut the view weight, and made
      youtube's own rank count for much more.
    * covers outranked originals, and the radio queue then
      followed the cover, so the whole session drifted. Cover,
      acoustic and unplugged are now penalised.

  checked by hand

    * hindi search in both scripts, correct song on top for
      लग जा गले, तेरे बिना जिया जाए ना, ओम जय जगदीश हरे,
      कभी कभी मेरे दिल में, मुझे माफ करना
    * fold: Devanagari query vs romanized title scores 1.00,
      wrong song 0.00
    * download gives AAC 128k m4a, 4.1 MiB for 4:11, in 5.6s
    * cache hit returns in 0.00s, no temp files left behind
    * signed url: valid passes, tampered 403, expired 403,
      wrong key 403
    * signature: forged CA rejected, tampered body rejected,
      cert url traversal rejected, missing SAN rejected, stale
      timestamp rejected
    * simulated conversation end to end: launch, play from a
      Devanagari fragment, Echo fetch 200 with audio/mp4, range
      206, PlaybackStarted, NearlyFinished returning ENQUEUE
      with the right expectedPreviousToken, next, pause
    * skill id mismatch 403, wrong Host 403, right Host 200
    * radio gave 50 era matched tracks from a Lata seed
    * env overrides cast ints and lists, and suppress the
      config file write when YTA_ADMIN_TOKEN is set

  known weak spots

    * romanized queries rank worse than Devanagari ones. Alexa
      hi-IN transcribes to Devanagari so the common case is the
      good one, but it is a real gap.
    * ranking is heuristic. The weights are one table at the top
      of yt_search.py and want tuning against real phrases.
    * nothing here has run on a real Echo or a real phone yet.


